  "text": "Australia\n\nA cholecystectomy is a surgical procedure to remove the gallbladder, which is commonly performed to resolve gallstones that cause pain and infection. It's often done laparoscopically, making it minimally invasive with a shorter recovery time. However, there are risks such as injury to the bile duct, infection, bleeding, and in rare cases, leakage of bile into the abdomen."
